content": [{"id": "toolu_01QvnpDwj3sonSJcsiKBB7oW", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01YZ8JtGUdkcV6c9qyU6JxES", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/money-round-half-even", "message": "Use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) in round_money per FIN-212", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01S6owTexpecee8UtHuWe5ax", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/money-round-half-even", "idempotency_key": "ci-fix-money-round-half-even-08d3cd5986"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_011mEy9CKt1pNjEtNFnPTyMD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014YkBxFuP1NDuWGxoyHLU46", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/money-round-half-even", "base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py` documented banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212) but actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, causing `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even` to fail in the nightly build (e.g. 2.665 rounded to 2.67 instead of 2.66).\n\nThis change switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 passed on 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-round-half-even"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and I opened PR #101 against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n**The bug:** In `src/money.py`, the comment on `round_money` says it uses banker's rounding (round half to even), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. So 2.665 came out as 2.67 instead of the 2.66 the test expects.\n\n**The fix:** On a new branch, `fix/money-round-half-even`, I changed it to use `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. That was the only change, one commit.\n\n**CI:** Run ci-0001 passed on that commit.\n\nThe FIN-212 lookup failed with \"Unknown advisory\", so I couldn't check the requirement against it. The fix is based on the comment in the code and what the test expects.\n\nThe PR still needs approval from a code owner before it can be merged, and I haven't merged it.", "type": "text"}]}]}